{
  "status": "Verified dashed polymer gaps; full Phase 3.1 remains open",
  "owner": "Phase 3.1",
  "source_before": "db31f963",
  "architecture": [
    "One GapStyle enum drives Rust configurations/builders, scene values, canonical restorable descriptions, command parser/printer, Python keyword/stubs and WASM serialization. All five polymer families share geometry.",
    "One ordered chain traversal finds canonical missing guide intervals, missing guide coordinates and spatial breaks over 8 \u00c5. Excluded existing guide atoms reset the interval. Chains and mixed polymer guide types never connect.",
    "Closed tubes use 0.15 \u00c5 radius and 0.5 \u00c5 dash/spacing. Existing spline scratch, deformation rows and beauty/OIT/shadow/picking shaders are reused. Source coordinates remain borrowed and source atom identity is retained.",
    "Resident frame endpoints bound maximum dash capacity by convexity of norm under linear interpolation. Sample-only updates deform resident vertices without traversal, rebuilding or uploading gap buffers. New coordinate intervals invalidate geometry; camera-only changes retain it.",
    "Preflight capacity rejects unrepresentable geometry before emission; failed appends roll back. Reserved invisible dashes collapse to zero-area triangles, avoiding ghosts and erroneous picks.",
    "Culling modes and dispatch resource types now have a separate cohesive module, keeping all Rust/WGSL source files within repository size limits."
  ],
  "complexity": "Cold traversal O(residues \u00d7 selection membership cost), geometry O(dashes), retained scratch O(samples) and output O(dashes). Each straight dash adds 66 vertices and 192 indices; no extra per-dash draw or GPU pass.",
